      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture. The original test has several understandability issues:\n- Unused static fields (`TEST_BOM_1/2/3`) and several unused imports add noise\n- A single monolithic test method bundles four distinct failure scenarios without explaining each\n- The inline lambdas give no hint of which invariant is being validated\n\nI'll improve it by removing dead code, splitting each scenario into its own descriptively-named test method, and cleaning up imports.The improved test compiles successfully. The refactored version removes the three unused static fields and six unused imports, then splits the original single monolithic test into four focused, self-describing test methods — one per constructor invariant — making it immediately clear which precondition each assertion validates."
    }
